From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: keys in pages repeat as the config says

The compositor tells native windows how held keys repeat from
`input.keyboard.repeat`. Pages repeat through Chromium's own
`KeyboardEvdev`, which kept its 500 ms and 20 a second.

- `SetDomicileInputConfig`: sets the auto-repeat delay and interval from
  the input settings' keyboard, and turns repeat off for a rate of 0.

---
 ui/events/ozone/evdev/input_controller_evdev.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/events/ozone/evdev/input_controller_evdev.cc b/ui/events/ozone/evdev/input_controller_evdev.cc
index 4a022b9..c828c70 100644
--- a/ui/events/ozone/evdev/input_controller_evdev.cc
+++ b/ui/events/ozone/evdev/input_controller_evdev.cc
@@ -244,6 +244,12 @@ void InputControllerEvdev::SetDomicileInputConfig(
     DomicileInputSettings settings) {
   input_device_settings_.domicile_disable_while_typing =
       settings.touchpad.disable_while_typing != DomicileTypingPolicy::kDisabled;
+  // Page key repeat, matching what the compositor tells native windows.
+  SetAutoRepeatEnabled(settings.keyboard.repeat_rate > 0);
+  if (settings.keyboard.repeat_rate > 0) {
+    SetAutoRepeatRate(settings.keyboard.repeat_delay,
+                      base::Seconds(1) / settings.keyboard.repeat_rate);
+  }
   input_device_settings_.domicile_input = std::move(settings);
   ++input_device_settings_.domicile_input_generation;
   ScheduleUpdateDeviceSettings();
